{"id":"1073978ace364aae0f729a6128cde21ffaea987f","axis":"silent","repo":"openvinotoolkit/openvino","sha":"1073978ace364aae0f729a6128cde21ffaea987f","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/articles_en/documentation/openvino-extensibility/openvino-plugin-library/compiled-model.rst","lines":["@@ -82,7 +82,7 @@ By default, the Template plugin exports an HSM blob: a container of sections. Th"," seekable. The blob has these sections:"," "," * model id and runtime requirements","-* compiled options: the values of the properties listed by ``ov::internal::caching_properties`` and","+* compile options: the values of the properties listed by ``ov::internal::caching_properties`` and","   ``ov::weights_path``, if it is set"," * model structure (XML) and weights"," * blob info, which tells if the weights are stored in the blob"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/articles_en/documentation/openvino-extensibility/openvino-plugin-library/plugin.rst","lines":["@@ -209,11 +209,11 @@ The import works in these steps:"," "," * The model structure and the blob info sections are mandatory."," * The blob is rejected if its runtime requirements are not supported by the plugin.","-* The compiled options are restored into the plugin configuration. Properties passed to","+* The compile options are restored into the plugin configuration. Properties passed to","   ``import_model`` have a higher priority."," * The weights are taken from the blob. If the blob has no weights section (for example, it was exported","   with ``ov::cache_mode(ov::CacheMode::OPTIMIZE_SIZE)``), they are read from ``ov::weights_path``,","-  or from the path stored in the compiled options.","+  or from the path stored in the compile options."," * Sections that the plugin does not know are skipped, so blobs written by a newer format minor version","   still import."," "],"additions":2,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/inference/dev_api/openvino/runtime/hsm_compile_options_codec.hpp","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,82 @@","+// Copyright (C) 2018-2026 Intel Corporation","+// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0","+//","+","+/**","+ * @brief Plugin-agnostic codec for the #compile_options_tag section payload.","+ * @file openvino/runtime/hsm_compile_options_codec.hpp","+ *","+ * The payload is one encoded `ov::AnyMap`, written and parsed as a stream - no lengths, no size limits:","+ * @verbatim","+   Payload  := Entry* FS digest","+   Entry    := Leaf | Map | Reserved","+   Leaf     := key US value US","+   Map      := key GS Entry* GS","+   Reserved := key RS content RS","+   @endverbatim","+ * - Separators: `US` = 0x1F, `GS` = 0x1D, `RS` = 0x1E, `FS` = 0x1C. `key` and `value` are byte strings","+ *   containing none of `NUL`, `US`, `GS`, `RS`, `FS`; `content` is any bytes except `RS` and `FS`.","+ * - A Leaf holds a string value, a Map a nested options map. Entries of one map are unique by key, whatever","+ *   their kind; they may come in any order.","+ * - An entry with an empty key is skipped by the decoder. A `GS` with no key bytes before it closes the current","+ *   map instead.","+ * - Reserved is for future extensions: the decoder skips it entirely, its key included; the encoder never writes it.","+ * - `digest` is 8 bytes in native byte order. Every payload byte before it, `FS` included, is packed into 64-bit","+ *   words (the first byte is the lowest; a trailing partial word is zero-padded); `h = 0`, then","+ *   `h = ov::util::u64_hash_combine(h, word)` for every word. It detects accidental corruption only. The section","+ *   size must be exactly the position of `FS` + 1 + 8.","+ */","+","+#pragma once","+","+#include <functional>","+#include <optional>","+","+#include \"openvino/core/any.hpp\"","+#include \"openvino/runtime/common.hpp\"","+#include \"openvino/runtime/hsm_reader.hpp\"","+#include \"openvino/runtime/hsm_writer.hpp\"","+","+namespace ov::runtime::hsm {","+inline namespace v1 {","+","+/**","+ * @brief #ISectionEncoder for a #compile_options_tag section: borrows @p options and writes them straight to the","+ * sink, with no intermediate buffer - for the unsized #IWriter::add_section() overload.","+ * @note The borrowed map must outlive #IWriter::finalize().","+ * @note Value types:","+ * - `std::string` is written as is;","+ * - `ov::AnyMap` and `std::map<std::string, ov::AnyMap>` (e.g. `ov::device::properties`) become nested maps;","+ * - any other value is written as its `ov::Any::print()` text in the classic \"C\" locale, floating-point values","+ *   with `max_digits10` digits.","+ * Such a value must read back unchanged through `ov::util::Read` - callbacks, pointers and tensors can't be","+ * stored, leave them out of @p options.","+ * @note Every nested map is decoded as `ov::AnyMap` and every leaf as `std::string`, whatever type was encoded.","+ */","+class OPENVINO_RUNTIME_API CompileOptionsEncoder final : public ISectionEncoder {","+public:","+    explicit CompileOptionsEncoder(const ov::AnyMap& options) noexcept : m_options{options} {}","+    explicit CompileOptionsEncoder(ov::AnyMap&&) = delete;","+    explicit CompileOptionsEncoder(const ov::AnyMap&&) = delete;","+","+    /**","+     * @throw ov::Exception if a key is empty, an `ov::Any` is empty, a key or value contains a reserved byte","+     * (`NUL`, `US`, `GS`, `RS`, `FS`), a non-string value has no text form, or its conversion throws. Part of the","+     * section may already be written to @p sink by then.","+     */","+    void encode(const SectionSink& sink) const override;","+","+private:","+    std::reference_wrapper<const ov::AnyMap> m_options;","+};","+","+/**","+ * @brief Decodes a #compile_options_tag payload.","+ * @param section Section to decode; its tag must be #compile_options_tag.","+ * @return Decoded options; `std::nullopt` if the section is malformed, the hash does not match, or a key appears","+ * more than once within the same map level (as a leaf, a nested map, or both).","+ */","+OPENVINO_RUNTIME_API std::optional<ov::AnyMap> decode_compile_options(const Section& section);","+","+}  // namespace v1","+}  // namespace ov::runtime::hsm"],"additions":82,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/inference/dev_api/openvino/runtime/hsm_format.hpp","lines":["@@ -272,7 +272,7 @@ enum class Tags : uint32_t {","     model = 2,                 //!< See #model.","     runtime_requirements = 3,  //!< See #runtime_requirements_tag.","     weights = 4,               //!< See #weights_tag.","-    compiled_options = 5,      //!< See #compiled_options_tag.","+    compile_options = 5,       //!< See #compile_options_tag.","     // Add new Core tags above this line only, each with the next explicit value - never change or reuse an","     // existing tag's value.","     sentinel_count,  // Not a real tag id - always exactly one past the last real entry above.","@@ -284,7 +284,7 @@ inline constexpr uint32_t model_id = static_cast<uint32_t>(Tags::model_id);  //!"," inline constexpr uint32_t model = static_cast<uint32_t>(Tags::model);        //!< The serialized compiled model itself."," inline constexpr uint32_t runtime_requirements = static_cast<uint32_t>(Tags::runtime_requirements);"," inline constexpr uint32_t weights = static_cast<uint32_t>(Tags::weights);","-inline constexpr uint32_t compiled_options = static_cast<uint32_t>(Tags::compiled_options);","+inline constexpr uint32_t compile_options = static_cast<uint32_t>(Tags::compile_options);"," "," /// Wire tag for #model_id - always inline-mode."," inline constexpr SectionTag model_id_tag = SectionTag::make(model_id, /*is_inline=*/true);","@@ -304,8 +304,8 @@ inline constexpr SectionTag runtime_requirements_tag = SectionTag::make(runtime_"," /// Wire tag for #weights - always pointer-mode. Payload contract: CVS-196451."," inline constexpr SectionTag weights_tag = SectionTag::make(weights, /*is_inline=*/false);"," ","-/// Wire tag for #compiled_options - always pointer-mode. Payload contract: CVS-196452.","-inline constexpr SectionTag compiled_options_tag = SectionTag::make(compiled_options, /*is_inline=*/false);","+/// Wire tag for #compile_options - always pointer-mode. Payload: see openvino/runtime/hsm_compile_options_codec.hpp.","+inline constexpr SectionTag compile_options_tag = SectionTag::make(compile_options, /*is_inline=*/false);"," "," /**","  * @brief One fixed-size, 32-byte record of the manifest table (see #Header::manifest_offset)."],"additions":4,"deletions":4,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/inference/sources.cmake","lines":["@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@ set(OV_RUNTIME_SRCS","     ${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/src/dev/core_impl.cpp","     ${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/src/dev/device_id_parser.cpp","     ${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/src/dev/exec_model_info.cpp","+    ${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/src/dev/hsm_compile_options_codec.cpp","     ${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/src/dev/hsm_format.cpp","     ${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/src/dev/hsm_deferred_writer.cpp","     ${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/src/dev/hsm_model_id_codec.cpp"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/inference/src/dev/hsm_compile_options_codec.cpp","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,358 @@","+// Copyright (C) 2018-2026 Intel Corporation","+// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0","+//","+","+#include \"openvino/runtime/hsm_compile_options_codec.hpp\"","+","+#include <algorithm>","+#include <array>","+#include <cstdint>","+#include <exception>","+#include <iomanip>","+#include <limits>","+#include <locale>","+#include <map>","+#include <optional>","+#include <sstream>","+#include <string>","+#include <string_view>","+#include <vector>","+","+#include \"openvino/core/except.hpp\"","+#include \"openvino/util/hash_util.hpp\"","+#include \"openvino/util/memory.hpp\"","+","+namespace ov::runtime::hsm {","+inline namespace v1 {","+namespace {","+","+constexpr char us = '\\x1f';  // ends a key and its value","+constexpr char gs = '\\x1d';  // opens and closes a nested map","+constexpr char rs = '\\x1e';  // opens and closes a reserved block","+constexpr char fs = '\\x1c';  // ends the entries","+constexpr std::string_view reserved_bytes{\"\\0\\x1f\\x1d\\x1e\\x1c\", 5};","+","+// Packs bytes into little-endian 64-bit words and folds every complete word into the hash.","+class HashAccumulator {","+public:","+    HashAccumulator() noexcept : m_hash{0}, m_word{0}, m_count{0} {}","+","+    void add(char byte) noexcept {","+        m_word |= static_cast<uint64_t>(static_cast<uint8_t>(byte)) << (8 * m_count);","+        if (++m_count == sizeof(m_word)) {","+            m_hash = ov::util::u64_hash_combine(m_hash, m_word);","+            m_word = 0;","+            m_count = 0;","+        }","+    }","+","+    void add(std::string_view bytes) noexcept {","+        for (const auto byte : bytes) {","+            add(byte);","+        }","+    }","+","+    // A trailing partial word is zero-padded; the accumulator itself is not changed.","+    uint64_t digest() const noexcept {","+        return m_count == 0 ? m_hash : ov::util::u64_hash_combine(m_hash, m_word);","+    }","+","+private:","+    uint64_t m_hash;","+    uint64_t m_word;","+    size_t m_count;","+};","+","+// Sends every piece to the sink and folds it into the digest that closes the payload.","+class HashingWriter {","+public:","+    explicit HashingWriter(const SectionSink& sink) noexcept : m_sink{sink} {}","+","+    void put(std::string_view bytes) {","+        if (!bytes.empty()) {","+            m_hash.add(bytes);","+            m_sink(ov::util::as_memory_view(bytes));","+        }","+    }","+","+    void put(char separator) {","+        put(std::string_view{&separator, 1});","+    }","+","+    void finish() {","+        put(fs);","+        const auto digest = m_hash.digest();","+        m_sink(ov::util::as_memory_view(digest));","+    }","+","+private:","+    const SectionSink& m_sink;","+    HashAccumulator m_hash;","+};","+","+void check_text(std::string_view what, std::string_view text, std::string_view key) {","+    OPENVINO_ASSERT(text.find_first_of(reserved_bytes) == std::string_view::npos,","+                    \"Compile option \",","+                    what,","+                    \" contains a reserved byte (NUL, 0x1C-0x1F), key: \",","+                    key);","+}","+","+template <class T>","+bool set_precision(std::ostream& os, const ov::Any& value) {","+    if (value.is<T>()) {","+        os << std::setprecision(std::numeric_limits<T>::max_digits10);","+        return true;","+    }","+    return false;","+}","+","+// Classic locale and max_digits10 keep the text deterministic and parseable back to the same value.","+std::string to_option_string(const ov::Any& value) {","+    std::ostringstream os;","+    os.imbue(std::locale::classic());","+    (set_precision<float>(os, value) || set_precision<double>(os, value) || set_precision<long double>(os, value));","+    value.print(os);","+    return os.str();","+}","+","+void write_key(HashingWriter& out, const std::string& key) {","+    OPENVINO_ASSERT(!key.empty(), \"Compile option key must not be empty\");","+    check_text(\"key\", key, key);","+    out.put(key);","+}","+","+void write_leaf(HashingWriter& out, const std::string& key, const std::string& text) {","+    write_key(out, key);","+    out.put(us);","+    check_text(\"value\", text, key);","+    out.put(text);","+    out.put(us);","+}","+","+void write_entries(HashingWriter& out, const ov::AnyMap& options);","+","+void write_nested(HashingWriter& out, const std::string& key, const ov::AnyMap& options) {","+    write_key(out, key);","+    out.put(gs);","+    write_entries(out, options);","+    out.put(gs);","+}","+","+void write_nested(HashingWriter& out, const std::string& key, const std::map<std::string, ov::AnyMap>& options) {","+    write_key(out, key);","+    out.put(gs);","+    for (const auto& [name, nested] : options) {","+        write_nested(out, name, nested);","+    }","+    out.put(gs);","+}","+","+void write_entries(HashingWriter& out, const ov::AnyMap& options) {","+    for (const auto& [key, value] : options) {","+        OPENVINO_ASSERT(!value.empty(), \"Compile option value must not be empty, key: \", key);","+","+        if (value.is<std::string>()) {","+            write_leaf(out, key, value.as<std::string>());","+        } else if (value.is<ov::AnyMap>()) {","+            write_nested(out, key, value.as<ov::AnyMap>());","+        } else if (value.is<std::map<std::string, ov::AnyMap>>()) {","+            write_nested(out, key, value.as<std::map<std::string, ov::AnyMap>>());","+        } else {","+            std::string text;","+            try {","+                text = to_option_string(value);","+            } catch (const std::exception& e) {","+                OPENVINO_THROW(\"Cannot convert compile option \", key, \" to string: \", e.what());","+            }","+            OPENVINO_ASSERT(!text.empty(),","+                            \"Compile option \",","+                            key,","+                            \" of type \",","+                            value.type_info().name(),","+                            \" has no string form\");","+            write_leaf(out, key, text);","+        }","+    }","+}","+","+enum class Status { more, done, malformed };","+","+/*","+ * Byte-at-a-time parser; open nested maps live on a heap stack so depth is bounded by memory, not the call stack.","+ *","+ *  state     byte          action                                          next","+ *  key       other         append to key                                   key","+ *            US            -                                               value","+ *            GS            key set: open nested map; key empty: close map  key","+ *            RS            drop key                                        reserved","+ *            FS            key empty at root: done; otherwise malformed    -","+ *            NUL           malformed                                       -","+ *  value     other         append to value                                 value","+ *            US            store leaf (duplicate key: malformed)           key","+ *            GS RS FS NUL  malformed                                       -","+ *  reserved  other         skip                                            reserved","+ *            RS            -                                               key","+ *            FS            malformed                                       -","+ */","+class Parser {","+public:","+    Parser() {","+        m_levels.emplace_back();","+    }","+","+    Status consume(char byte) {","+        switch (m_state) {","+        case State::key:","+            return on_key(byte);","+        case State::value:","+            return on_value(byte);","+        default:","+            return on_reserved(byte);","+        }","+    }","+","+    ov::AnyMap take() {","+        return std::move(m_levels.front().options);","+    }","+","+private:","+    enum class State { key, value, reserved };","+","+    struct Level {","+        std::string name;","+        ov::AnyMap options;","+    };","+","+    Status on_key(char byte) {","+        switch (byte) {","+        case us:","+            m_state = State::value;","+            return Status::more;","+        case gs:","+            return m_key.empty() ? close_level() : open_level();","+        case rs:","+            m_key.clear();","+            m_state = State::reserved;","+            return Status::more;","+        case fs:","+            return m_key.empty() && m_levels.size() == 1 ? Status::done : Status::malformed;","+        case '\\0':","+            return Status::malformed;","+        default:","+            m_key.push_back(byte);","+            return Status::more;","+        }","+    }","+","+    Status on_value(char byte) {","+        switch (byte) {","+        case us:","+            if (!m_key.empty() && !m_levels.back().options.emplace(m_key, ov::Any{std::move(m_value)}).second) {","+                return Status::malformed;","+            }","+            m_key.clear();","+            m_value.clear();","+            m_state = State::key;","+            return Status::more;","+        case gs:","+        case rs:","+        case fs:","+        case '\\0':","+            return Status::malformed;","+        default:","+            m_value.push_back(byte);","+            return Status::more;","+        }","+    }","+","+    Status on_reserved(char byte) {","+        if (byte == fs) {","+            return Status::malformed;","+        } else if (byte == rs) {","+            m_state = State::key;","+        }","+        return Status::more;","+    }","+","+    // The key is checked here, not when the map closes: nothing else can add to this level meanwhile.","+    Status open_level() {","+        if (m_levels.back().options.count(m_key) != 0) {","+            return Status::malformed;","+        }","+        m_levels.push_back({std::move(m_key), {}});","+        m_key.clear();","+        return Status::more;","+    }","+","+    Status close_level() {","+        if (m_levels.size() == 1) {","+            return Status::malformed;","+        }","+        auto level = std::move(m_levels.back());","+        m_levels.pop_back();","+        m_levels.back().options.emplace(std::move(level.name), ov::Any{std::move(level.options)});","+        return Status::more;","+    }","+","+    State m_state = State::key;","+    std::string m_key;","+    std::string m_value;","+    std::vector<Level> m_levels;","+};","+","+constexpr size_t chunk_size = ov::util::min_page_alignment;","+","+}  // namespace","+","+void CompileOptionsEncoder::encode(const SectionSink& sink) const {","+    HashingWriter out{sink};","+    write_entries(out, m_options.get());","+    out.finish();","+}","+","+std::optional<ov::AnyMap> decode_compile_options(const Section& section) {","+    const auto size = section.size();","+    if (size == 0) {","+        return std::nullopt;","+    }","+","+    std::array<std::byte, chunk_size> chunk;","+    Parser parser;","+    HashAccumulator hash;","+","+    const auto view = section.view();","+    ov::util::MemoryView block = view;","+    for (size_t offset = 0; offset < size;) {","+        if (view.empty()) {  // No addressable memory (stream-backed): copy the next chunk.","+            const auto count = std::min(chunk.size(), size - offset);","+            if (!section.read(offset, count, chunk.data())) {","+                return std::nullopt;","+            }","+            block = {chunk.data(), count};","+        }","+","+        for (size_t i = 0; i < block.size(); ++i) {","+            const auto byte = static_cast<char>(block.data()[i]);","+            hash.add(byte);","+            switch (parser.consume(byte)) {","+            case Status::more:","+                break;","+            case Status::malformed:","+                return std::nullopt;","+            case Status::done: {","+                const auto digest_offset = offset + i + 1;","+                uint64_t digest = 0;","+                const auto is_valid = size - digest_offset == sizeof(digest) &&","+                                      section.read(digest_offset, sizeof(digest), &digest) && digest == hash.digest();","+                return is_valid ? std::optional{parser.take()} : std::nullopt;","+            }","+            }","+        }","+        offset += block.size();","+    }","+    return std::nullopt;","+}","+","+}  // namespace v1","+}  // namespace ov::runtime::hsm"],"additions":358,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/inference/tests/unit/CMakeLists.txt","lines":["@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@ ov_add_test_target(","             ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/cpu_stream_info_test.cpp","             ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/executor_config_test.cpp","             ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/executor_manager_tests.cpp","+            ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/hsm_compile_options_codec.cpp","             ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/hsm_deferred_writer.cpp","             ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/hsm_format.cpp","             ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/hsm_model_id_codec.cpp"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/inference/tests/unit/hsm_compile_options_codec.cpp","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,843 @@","+// Copyright (C) 2018-2026 Intel Corporation","+// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0","+//","+","+#include \"openvino/runtime/hsm_compile_options_codec.hpp\"","+","+#include <gtest/gtest.h>","+","+#include <cmath>","+#include <cstdint>","+#include <ios>","+#include <limits>","+#include <locale>","+#include <map>","+#include <memory>","+#include <optional>","+#include <ostream>","+#include <set>","+#include <sstream>","+#include <stdexcept>","+#include <streambuf>","+#include <string>","+#include <string_view>","+#include <type_traits>","+#include <utility>","+#include <vector>","+","+#include \"openvino/core/type/element_type.hpp\"","+#include \"openvino/runtime/hsm_format.hpp\"","+#include \"openvino/runtime/hsm_reader.hpp\"","+#include \"openvino/runtime/hsm_writer.hpp\"","+#include \"openvino/runtime/properties.hpp\"","+#include \"openvino/util/hash_util.hpp\"","+#include \"openvino/util/memory.hpp\"","+","+namespace ov::test {","+namespace hsm = ov::runtime::hsm;","+using namespace std::string_literals;","+namespace {","+","+static_assert(std::is_convertible_v<decltype(&hsm::decode_compile_options), hsm::SectionDecoder<ov::AnyMap>>,","+              \"decode_compile_options(const Section&) must be usable as a SectionDecoder<ov::AnyMap>.\");","+static_assert(std::is_base_of_v<hsm::ISectionEncoder, hsm::CompileOptionsEncoder>,","+              \"CompileOptionsEncoder must be an ISectionEncoder.\");","+static_assert(std::is_convertible_v<std::shared_ptr<hsm::CompileOptionsEncoder>, hsm::SectionEncoderPtr>,","+              \"CompileOptionsEncoder must be passable as a SectionEncoderPtr.\");","+static_assert(std::is_constructible_v<hsm::CompileOptionsEncoder, const ov::AnyMap&>,","+              \"CompileOptionsEncoder must borrow an existing map.\");","+static_assert(!std::is_constructible_v<hsm::CompileOptionsEncoder, ov::AnyMap&&>,","+              \"CompileOptionsEncoder must not borrow a temporary map.\");","+static_assert(!std::is_constructible_v<hsm::CompileOptionsEncoder, const ov::AnyMap&&>,","+              \"CompileOptionsEncoder must not borrow a temporary const map.\");","+static_assert(std::is_same_v<decltype(std::declval<hsm::IWriter&>().add_section(","+                                 hsm::DeviceId{},","+                                 hsm::compile_options_tag,","+                                 std::declval<std::shared_ptr<hsm::CompileOptionsEncoder>>())),","+                             bool>,","+              \"CompileOptionsEncoder must fit the unsized IWriter::add_section(SectionEncoderPtr).\");","+","+constexpr hsm::DeviceId fake_device_id = hsm::private_device_id_range_start + 42;","+constexpr size_t chunk_size = ov::util::min_page_alignment;","+","+// Separators, spelled out here on purpose - the codec's own constants are not visible to the tests.","+const std::string US{\"\\x1f\"};","+const std::string GS{\"\\x1d\"};","+const std::string RS{\"\\x1e\"};","+const std::string FS{\"\\x1c\"};","+","+// The digest rule from the format description, applied to everything up to and including FS.","+std::string digest_of(std::string_view bytes) {","+    constexpr size_t word_size = sizeof(uint64_t);","+    uint64_t hash = 0;","+    for (size_t pos = 0; pos < bytes.size(); pos += word_size) {","+        uint64_t word = 0;","+        for (size_t i = 0; i < word_size && pos + i < bytes.size(); ++i) {","+            word |= static_cast<uint64_t>(static_cast<uint8_t>(bytes[pos + i])) << (8 * i);","+        }","+        hash = ov::util::u64_hash_combine(hash, word);","+    }","+    return std::string{reinterpret_cast<const char*>(&hash), sizeof(hash)};","+}","+","+// @p body must end with FS.","+std::string with_digest(const std::string& body) {","+    return body + di